{"id": "swebq0148", "pool": "swebq", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 1391819813, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "aa7a8a6f2040793a4fe8dabcb6d10f2520887b0e0988d37809c3a27ef31575d8", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 7, "query": "what languages do they speak in costa rica?", "input_path": "/data/bench_audio/swebq0148.wav", "input_sha256": "251ba5b0c1d1e2c7fcfa000a2b9783d0b0774c3164862f2dfca2c2d6d7985e9c", "input_samples": 39363, "input_s": 2.46, "n_real_chunks": 3, "score": 0.51, "act": 0.9981, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "In Costa Rica, the official language is Spanish. Other languages spoken include: English — especially in tourism and by some communities on the Caribbean coast , Costa Rican Sign Language , Indigenous languages, including Bribri, Cabécar, Maléku, Ngäbere, and Buglere , Mekatelyu / Costa Rican Creole English — spoken mainly in Afro-Caribbean communities around Limón.", "expert_answer": "In **Costa Rica**, the official language is **Spanish**.\n\nOther languages spoken include:\n\n- **English** — especially in tourism and by some communities on the Caribbean coast\n- **Costa Rican Sign Language**\n- **Indigenous languages**, including **Bribri**, **Cabécar**, **Maléku**, **Ngäbere**, and **Buglere**\n- **Mekatelyu / Costa Rican Creole English** — spoken mainly in Afro-Caribbean communities around Limón.", "transcript": "What languages do they speak in Costa Rica?\n", "asr_s": 0.62, "expert_s": 3.13, "expert_input_samples": 39363, "expert_input_s": 2.46, "expert_input_sha256": "251ba5b0c1d1e2c7fcfa000a2b9783d0b0774c3164862f2dfca2c2d6d7985e9c", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 2.946, "relay_synth_ms": 15800, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 0, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 